{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And every offering of your meal offering you shall salt with salt</b> — three times salt is mentioned in the verse, because in three places the salt is placed: in the Chamber of Salt, and on the ramp, and on the altar." "<b>you shall offer salt</b> — in gematria this equals: he brings salt from the public's [funds]."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The Kitzur treats the threefold mention of מלח in the verse as corresponding to three physical locations where salt was placed in the Temple precincts.", 1 "The gematria of תקריב מלח equals זה יביא מלח משל ציבור, teaching that salt for offerings is purchased communally rather than by the individual offerer."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:19:54.781235449Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}